On Tue, 25 Nov 2003, Don Cohen wrote:

> Once again I send something to netfilter-devel and start getting
> spam.  I know it's due to this list cause it's to this address which
> I use for only this mailing list.

This is a common problem with most large or well known mailinglists.. some
of the spammers have robots which actively subscribe to mailinglists to
collect email information, and they also harvest the same information from 
different mail archives.

I would recommend the use of spamassassin. It very effectively takes care
of the spam problem with much less false decisions than manually trying to
wade thru the crap until the legal systems catch up making it somewhat
more effective to try to go after the spammers. I currenly receive about
4000 spam/month on the addresses I use, and maybe 20 or so ends up in my
mailbox..

